abstract: >-
  Four Colab notebooks and their worksheets for computer-aided molecular
  design: molecular interactions, structural validity and alerts, bioisosteric
  replacement, and retrosynthesis. Usable for research as well as teaching --
  the structural validation module reports the specific atom at fault and
  explains why rather than returning a pass or fail, and includes a batch mode
  that reports validity rate and the breakdown of failure modes across a set of
  generated structures. Each module ships a worksheet that asks the user to
  predict before running and to judge what the tool cannot tell them. Built
  with RDKit; everything runs in Google Colab with no local installation.
